        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "593619be-0bd8-5397-be38-e94619187c64",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: New York–New Jersey Line War\n- Places: Province of New York, Province of New Jersey, New York City\n- People: John Cruger Jr.\n- Roles: Speaker of the Province of New York assembly, Mayor of New York City\n\nFacts:\n- The Province of New York was a British proprietary colony and later a royal colony on the northeast coast of North America from 1664 to 1776.\n- The New York–New Jersey Line War was a series of skirmishes and raids that occurred at the disputed border between the Province of New York and the Province of New Jersey from 1701 to 1765.\n- The New York–New Jersey Line War was also known as the N.J. Line War.\n- John Cruger Jr. was born on July 18, 1710, and died on December 27, 1791.\n- John Cruger Jr. served as speaker of the Province of New York assembly.\n- John Cruger Jr. was the 41st Mayor of New York City.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
